TVLWeightedContainers::deactivateContainer()
├── when container is not active
│   └── it should revert with TVLWeightedContainersInvalidInput
├── when container ID does not exist in active list
│   └── it should revert with TVLWeightedContainersInvalidInput
├── when container is active
│   ├── it should set container isActive to false
│   ├── it should remove container from activeContainerIds array
│   └── it should emit ContainerDeactivated event
├── when testing array integrity with multiple containers
│   ├── when deactivating middle container
│   │   └── it should maintain array integrity and keep other containers active
│   ├── when deactivating first container in array
│   │   └── it should remove first container and maintain others
│   ├── when deactivating last container in array
│   │   └── it should remove last container and maintain others
│   └── when deactivating all containers
│       └── it should result in empty active container array
└── when container is already deactivated
    └── it should revert with TVLWeightedContainersInvalidInput
